§§ `s 174`
-- s 174 illus (a): A, legally bound to appear before the General Division of the High Court in
-- obedience to an order to attend court issuing from it, intentionally omits to appear.
-- The High Court's order issues from a judge - a public servant (s 21(1)(b)) legally competent to issue it.
`174 illus (a)` MEANS `Failure to Attend Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `sample particulars`
    `the accused is an individual` IS TRUE
    `legally bound to attend in person or by an agent at a certain place and time` IS TRUE
    `in obedience to a summons, a notice, an order or a proclamation` IS TRUE
    `public servant` IS TRUE
    `the public servant` IS `nobody`
    `legally competent, as such public servant, to issue the same` IS TRUE
    intentionally IS TRUE
    `omits to attend at the place or time` IS TRUE
    `departs from the place before the time at which it is lawful to depart` IS FALSE
    `the summons, notice, order or proclamation is to attend in person or by agent before a court` IS TRUE
    `the process` IS "an order to attend court issuing from the General Division of the High Court"
    `to wit` IS ""
-- s 174 illus (a)
#ASSERT `offence under s 174(1)` `174 illus (a)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 174(2)` `174 illus (a)`
-- s 174 illus (b): A, legally bound to appear before a Magistrate as a witness, in obedience to
-- a summons issued by that Magistrate, intentionally omits to appear.
`174 illus (b)` MEANS `Failure to Attend Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `sample particulars`
    `the accused is an individual` IS TRUE
    `legally bound to attend in person or by an agent at a certain place and time` IS TRUE
    `in obedience to a summons, a notice, an order or a proclamation` IS TRUE
    `public servant` IS TRUE
    `the public servant` IS `nobody`
