§§ `s 177`
-- s 177 illus: A, a landholder, knowing of the commission of a murder within the limits of his
-- commercial property, intentionally misinforms the police that the death has occurred by accident in
-- consequence of the bite of a snake. The illustration presupposes that A was legally bound to inform.
`177 illus` MEANS `False Information Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `sample particulars`
    `the accused is an individual` IS TRUE
    `legally bound to furnish information on any subject` IS TRUE
    `to any public servant, as such` IS TRUE
    `public servant` IS TRUE
    `the public servant` IS `Sergeant Lim`
    `furnishes, as true, information on the subject` IS TRUE
    `knows the information to be false` IS TRUE
    `has reason to believe the information to be false` IS FALSE
    `the information respects the commission of an offence, or is required for the purpose of preventing the commission of an offence, or in order to the apprehension of an offender` IS TRUE
    `the information` IS "that the death had occurred by accident in consequence of the bite of a snake"
    `to wit` IS ""
-- s 177 illus
#ASSERT `offence under s 177(1)` `177 illus`
#ASSERT `offence under s 177(2)` `177 illus`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 177(2)` `177 illus`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 177(2)` `177 illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 3rd day of March 2026, at about 10.15 am, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being legally bound to furnish information to one Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division, a public servant, did furnish, as true, information that the death had occurred by accident in consequence of the bite of a snake, which you knew to be false, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 177(2)(a) of the Penal Code 1871."

