§§ `s 186`
-- s 186 illus: A tells SCDF paramedics on their way to a heart-attack patient that the lift has
-- broken down, knowing it false; they take the stairs and arrive 15 minutes later. "A has voluntarily
-- obstructed the paramedics in the discharge of their public function." s 186(2): no physical means needed.
`186 illus` MEANS `Obstructing Public Servant Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `sample particulars`
    `the accused is an individual` IS TRUE
    voluntarily IS TRUE
    obstructs IS TRUE
    `public servant` IS TRUE
    `the public servant` IS `Lieutenant Siti`
    `in the discharge of the public servant's public functions` IS TRUE
    `to wit` IS "by telling the paramedics that the lift had broken down, knowing this to be false"
-- s 186 illus
#ASSERT `voluntarily obstructs a public servant` `186 illus`
#ASSERT `offence under s 186` `186 illus`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 186` `186 illus`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 186` `186 illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 3rd day of March 2026, at about 10.15 am, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, did voluntarily obstruct one Siti binte Rahman, a paramedic of the Singapore Civil Defence Force, a public servant, in the discharge of her public functions, to wit, by telling the paramedics that the lift had broken down, knowing this to be false, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 186(1)(a) of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 186` `186 illus`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with both"
-- the same obstruction, not voluntary: refused, and the refusal names the missing element
`186: an accidental obstruction` MEANS `Obstructing Public Servant Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `sample particulars`
    `the accused is an individual` IS TRUE
    voluntarily IS FALSE
    obstructs IS TRUE
    `public servant` IS TRUE
    `the public servant` IS `Lieutenant Siti`
    `in the discharge of the public servant's public functions` IS TRUE
    `to wit` IS ""
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 186` `186: an accidental obstruction`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 186` `186: an accidental obstruction`)'s text EQUALS ""
#ASSERT (`charge under s 186` `186: an accidental obstruction`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 186(1)(a) would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of obstructing a public servant in the discharge of public functions (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: voluntarily; the elements of section 186 taken together."
-- s 41 over the punishment data: s 186(1)(a) is punishable with imprisonment for 6 months or upwards; s 186(1)(b) is not punishable with imprisonment at all
#ASSERT `punishable with imprisonment for` 6 `months or upwards within section 41` `punishment prescribed by s 186(1)(a)`
#ASSERT NOT `punishable with imprisonment for` 7 `months or upwards within section 41` `punishment prescribed by s 186(1)(a)`
#ASSERT NOT `punishable with imprisonment` `punishment prescribed by s 186(1)(b)`

