§§ `s 161`
-- s 161 illus (a): A, a judge, obtains from Z, a banker, a situation in Z's bank for A's brother, as a
-- reward to A for deciding a cause in favour of Z. The Explanation: a gratification need not be money.
`161 illus (a)` MEANS `Official Gratification Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `sample particulars`
    `public servant` IS TRUE
    `expecting to be a public servant` IS FALSE
    accepts IS FALSE
    obtains IS TRUE
    `agrees to accept` IS FALSE
    `attempts to obtain` IS FALSE
    `any gratification whatever` IS TRUE
    `other than legal remuneration` IS TRUE
    `as a motive or reward` IS TRUE
    `for doing or forbearing to do any official act` IS TRUE
    `for showing or forbearing to show, in the exercise of his official functions, favour or disfavour to any person` IS FALSE
    `for rendering or attempting to render any service or disservice to any person, with the Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such` IS FALSE
    `the giver` IS `Z`
    `the gratification` IS "a situation in the bank of the said Zainal bin Osman for your brother"
    `the official act` IS "for deciding a cause in favour of the said Zainal bin Osman"
    `to wit` IS ""
-- s 161 illus (a)
#ASSERT `offence under s 161` `161 illus (a)`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 161` `161 illus (a)`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 3rd day of March 2026, at about 10.15 am, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being a public servant, did obtain from one Zainal bin Osman, a gratification other than legal remuneration, namely a situation in the bank of the said Zainal bin Osman for your brother, as a motive or reward for deciding a cause in favour of the said Zainal bin Osman, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 161 of the Penal Code 1871."
